# `todo/t1077` REGRESSION CELL — payload: USER STRUCT,
# consume shape: FIELD READ through the nested box.
#
# ⭐ THE SAME PAYLOAD HAS TWO DIFFERENT FACES DEPENDING ON THE CONSUME SHAPE,
# which is why the discriminator is `payload type × consume shape × storage
# class` and not payload type alone. Read a FIELD and it is silent-wrong; read
# the WHOLE VALUE (`box_nested_deref_struct_whole_value_read.gg`) and the same
# program SIGSEGVs. A fixture set varying only the payload would have shown one
# of the two and called the axis covered.
#
#   PRE-fix, C:    build rc 0, run rc 0, prints `0` / `0`  ← SILENT WRONG
#   PRE-fix, LLVM: build rc 0, run rc 0, prints `0` / `0`  ← SILENT WRONG
#
# Silent-wrong-output outranks ICE on the severity ladder, and this cell plus
# `box_nested_deref_rodata_string_print.gg` are why `t1077`'s filed severity
# text ("SIGSEGV on C, silent wrong answer on LLVM") understated the class:
# here BOTH lanes are silently wrong.
#
# EXPECTED OUTPUT: 7 then 9
# EXPECTED EXIT: 0 on BOTH backends.
#
# ⛔ `known_gaps/` with a LIVE test: self-host cannot compile nested `Box`
# (`todo/t1311`) AND this leaks at scope exit (`todo/t1309`).

struct P:
    int x
    int y

void main():
    Box[Box[P]] w = Box[Box[P]](Box[P](P(7, 9)))
    print((*(*w)).x)
    print((*(*w)).y)
